  cal-20261002-s7-001,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Since answering session 6 tonight, have I done any of the three things it left for tonight: message a friend, reconstruct the day, or name the strength days?","I endorsed all three at about 21:45 on 2 October; session 6 offered to hold session 7 until one was done. Source: session 6.",keep generating each session as soon as the last is recorded,open session 8 only after one of them is done,calibration,88,82,70,88,92,exploit,"Resolved by my answer, as a fact about today.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-002,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Would a page on my site that solves a frame with Pynite in the reader's browser serve beamdiag's users better than extending beamdiag's own solver?,"I never thought my static site could run a Python FEA library; Pyodide loads Pynite with micropip, and a test solved a 6 m beam in 8 seconds. Source: Pyodide, Pynite.",brief a crewmate by 9 October for a one-page Pynite-in-the-browser prototype,keep extending beamdiag's own solver,news,90,88,96,72,92,explore,Resolved by a later note comparing the prototype with beamdiag for one engineer or one test case; unresolved otherwise.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-003,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would SymPy's beam solver, which solves statically indeterminate beams exactly, catch an error in beamdiag's hand-calculation export in five test cases?","My tools are checked only by their own tests. In a browser test SymPy's Beam class gave a propped cantilever's reactions as 75/2, 45/2 and 45. Source: SymPy docs.",have a crewmate run five beamdiag cases against SymPy by 16 October,keep beamdiag's own tests,news,86,82,92,80,90,explore,"Resolved by a note on the comparison by 2026-10-31: true if a mismatch traces to beamdiag.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-004,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Is the line I draw between people I know and strangers, rather than between one person and a crowd?","I turned down lecturers, a tutor and Show HN, but endorsed a mentor call and sending a mathematician my note. Source: my notes, 2 October.",send one piece of work to one named stranger by 16 October,post one piece of work to a forum by 16 October,synthesis,86,76,80,86,88,explore,Resolved by a later note recording either action and the reply; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-005,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would looking up one elliptic curve in the LMFDB, by 9 October, make the Weil conjectures that étale cohomology proves concrete faster than reading about them?","I learn étale cohomology from books. The LMFDB lists each curve's point counts and L-function, the numbers its H^1 predicts. Source: LMFDB.",look up curve 11.a2 and write what H^1 predicts by 9 October,keep to the reading,news,84,76,94,70,90,explore,Resolved by a later note on the look-up; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-006,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Do I endorse out-of-pattern cards I will not do, because endorsing them feels like doing them?","I endorsed 19 in session 6, 16 of them due within ten days. Source: session 6.",pick three of the 19 tonight and drop the rest in a note,keep all 19,calibration,86,84,74,94,90,exploit,"Resolved by a note by 2026-10-16 counting session 6's endorsed out-of-pattern actions done: true if fewer than three.",2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-007,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would running ccusage tonight, which reads Claude Code's local logs and reports cost by day, show a day in September costing more than I would guess?","I set the spend cap without looking at the bills. ccusage needs no account; one command reads the logs already on my Mac. Source: ccusage.",run it tonight and note my guess and the top day,"set the cap without looking, as planned",news,82,80,92,80,88,explore,"Resolved by a note by 2026-10-09 with my guess and the top day: true if the top day exceeds the guess.",2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-008,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Should site code changes keep the full no-mistakes pipeline through November?,"Session 5 gave 85% that Kun Chen's case against reviewing agents' PRs applies to my site; session 6 gave 16% to dropping no-mistakes for code. Source: my notes.",keep it through November and say so in a note,drop it for code changes and keep CI as the gate,calibration,84,82,62,86,90,exploit,"Resolved by the site's skills on 2026-11-30: true if code changes still take the full pipeline.",2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-009,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would a JupyterLite notebook of my statically indeterminate beams recap, which readers could edit and rerun in the browser, teach more than its deck?","I publish decks and videos. JupyterLite runs a full Jupyter from static files, so a reader could change a load and rerun. Source: JupyterLite docs.",brief a crewmate for one JupyterLite notebook by 16 October,keep decks,news,80,76,92,70,86,explore,Resolved by a later note comparing the notebook with the deck; unresolved otherwise.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-010,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Since session 6, have I asked one of the people closest to me whether I was less present this week?","Endorsed in session 5 (88%) and session 6 (81%); no note records asking. Source: my notes.",write down what they said in a note tonight,ask before answering session 8,calibration,84,82,64,96,88,exploit,"Resolved by my answer, as a fact about today.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-011,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would querying raw.toon with SQL in Datasette Lite, which runs in the browser from a static file, answer a question about my calibration that my notes cannot?","I read my history through agents' notes. Datasette Lite opens a CSV or SQLite file by URL and runs SQL in the page. Source: Datasette Lite.",have a crewmate publish raw.toon as CSV and open it in Datasette Lite by 16 October,keep reading it through notes,news,80,72,90,70,86,explore,Resolved by a later note naming such a question and its answer; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-012,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Are cards showing ways I did not know were possible more useful to me than out-of-pattern habit cards?,"Session 6's habit cards drew 19 yes and 24 no; card 020, a capability I had not known of, drew 100. Source: session 6.",make most out-of-pattern cards such ways from session 8,keep the mix as in session 7,calibration,86,78,80,74,90,explore,Resolved by a note after session 8 judging which kind changed more of what I did; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-013,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would a comment left on one Stacks Project tag in its étale-cohomology chapter, by 31 October, get a reply from its maintainers?","I learn from books alone. The Stacks Project, a free open textbook edited by Johan de Jong, takes comments on every result. Source: Stacks Project.",leave one comment by 31 October,keep my questions in my notes,news,80,74,94,80,84,explore,"Resolved by a note by 2026-11-30: true if it records a reply to my comment.",2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-014,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Did I want session 7 tonight more than I wanted to do session 6's actions?,"I gave 22% that I had done any of session 5's five, whose low action was to hold session 7, and asked for it the same evening. Source: session 6.",do one of session 6's actions before answering card 20,keep answering first,calibration,82,78,74,96,86,exploit,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note gives the reason; then resolved by it.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-015,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would checking my hand-derived one-loop QED beta function against PyR@TE 3, which computes gauge theories' renormalisation-group equations, find a factor I got wrong?","I redo physics by hand only; December starts from the renormalisation group. PyR@TE is open-source Python and handles U(1). Source: PyR@TE 3.",run PyR@TE on a QED model by 31 October,trust the hand derivation,news,80,72,94,76,82,explore,"Resolved by a note by 2026-12-31: true if it records a mismatch traced to my derivation.",2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-016,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would computing the vacuum-polarisation Dirac trace with SymPy's gamma-matrix module, before December, save more than an hour of hand algebra?","My physics is done by hand. SymPy's physics.hep module simplifies gamma-matrix traces and runs in a browser page. Source: SymPy docs.",try the trace in SymPy by 31 October,do it by hand in December,news,74,66,90,66,80,explore,Resolved by a later note comparing the two; unresolved otherwise.,2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-017,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would one 50-minute Focusmate session, silent video co-working with a stranger, for the first mathematics block, get more done than the block alone?","I work alone and turn down strangers who judge; here they only watch. Three sessions a week are free. Source: Focusmate.",book one for the first block,keep blocks alone,news,78,72,94,78,80,explore,Resolved by a later note comparing the session with a block alone; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-018,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would speaking first-hand observations into my phone, transcribed by whisper.cpp on my Mac, get me three a week more often than typing?","My first-hand notes lag behind agents'. whisper.cpp transcribes speech locally, with no cloud service. Source: whisper.cpp.",record the first observation by voice on 5 October,keep typing them,news,76,74,90,66,84,explore,"Resolved by notes to 2026-10-31: true if each week has three observations and at least one was dictated.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-019,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Have I booked the first mathematics block for Saturday 3 October?,"Session 6 endorsed booking it, at 23%. Source: session 6.",hold it before launching any crewmate on Saturday,book it for Sunday 4 October tonight,calibration,80,82,58,84,90,exploit,"Resolved by my answer, as a fact about today.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-020,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would splitting my Brier score into reliability and resolution, Murphy's 1973 method, show that most of it comes from easy questions?","My score is 0.167 over 36, most decided early. Weather forecasters separate calibration from discrimination this way. Source: Murphy 1973.",add the split to the October monthly note,report the Brier score alone,news,78,64,88,74,86,explore,"Resolved by the October monthly note if it reports the split: true if it judges the score flattered by easy questions.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-021,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would asking in Pynite's GitHub Discussions, by 9 October, whether a browser example through Pyodide is welcome make my pull request likelier to merge?","I gave 100% to an example pull request. Maintainers often say up front what they will take. Source: Pynite.",ask by 9 October,open the pull request without asking,news,76,74,86,66,86,explore,"Resolved by the Pynite repository: true if my pull request merges by 2026-12-31 after such a discussion; unresolved if none is opened.",2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
