  cal-20261002-s7-024,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would Hypothesis, a Python library that generates thousands of random test cases, find a beam where beamdiag and Pynite disagree?","I test tools on cases I choose. Property-based testing searches for a failing case and shrinks it to the simplest. Source: Hypothesis docs.",have a crewmate run it against Pynite by 31 October,keep hand-picked cases,news,76,70,90,74,84,explore,"Resolved by a note on the run by 2026-11-30: true if it finds a disagreement traced to beamdiag.",2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-025,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will two crewmates deploy the site at the same time in October?,"Deploys run from local checkouts; the playbook has no lock against a second one. Source: deploy playbook.",add a deploy lock,rely on checking other lanes' status,project,80,72,40,74,86,exploit,Resolved true if a note or commit by 2026-10-31 records overlapping deploys; false if a note judges none did.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-026,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would comparing sectionlab with sectionproperties, an open-source Python finite-element section analyser, for three sections find a difference above 1%?","sectionlab has no outside check. sectionproperties computes the same properties, with warping and shear centre, by finite elements. Source: sectionproperties.",have a crewmate compare three sections by 16 October,keep sectionlab's own tests,news,78,72,88,74,84,explore,"Resolved by a note on the comparison by 2026-10-31: true if a difference above 1% traces to sectionlab.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
