  cal-20261002-s7-046,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would trying to prove each lemma before reading its proof, in the weekday étale readings, help me remember more than reading straight through?","I read proofs as written. Generating an answer before seeing it improved memory over reading it. Source: Slamecka 1978.",try it from 5 October,read straight through,news,70,64,82,66,80,explore,Resolved by a later note comparing the two; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-047,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will I do the 20-minute étale reading on at least three of the five weekdays from 5 October?,"Endorsed tonight (86%), changing November's one-field plan. Source: my notes.",keep it at 20 minutes,make it 10 minutes,notes,72,70,56,70,86,exploit,"Resolved by notes by 2026-10-11: true if three readings are recorded.",2026-10-11,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-048,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would giscus, which adds comments to static pages through GitHub Discussions, bring at least one comment on a blog post by 31 December?","My site has no way for readers to reply. giscus needs no server. Source: giscus.",brief a crewmate to add it to blog posts by 31 October,keep the site without comments,news,68,62,86,70,78,explore,"Resolved by the site: true if a blog post has a comment by 2026-12-31; false if giscus is added and none comes.",2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-049,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Have I been answering Calibrator late in the day, when I can do least about it until tomorrow?","Session 6 ran from about 20:48 to 21:45 Singapore time. Source: session 6.",answer session 8 before noon,keep answering when it arrives,calibration,74,66,74,84,82,exploit,"Resolved by my answer, as a fact about today.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-050,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would one curve's point counts over small fields, computed in SageMathCell, show me the Weil bound in under an hour?","I do mathematics by hand. SageMathCell runs Sage in a web page with nothing installed. Source: SageMathCell.",count points of one curve for p up to 50 by 16 October,keep it on paper,news,70,62,88,62,82,explore,Resolved by a later note on the computation; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-051,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will the first monthly meal with a friend be booked by 9 October?,"Endorsed tonight (82%). Source: my notes.",keep it as a note,make it a dated todo tonight,notes,70,72,56,72,82,exploit,"Resolved by a note by 2026-10-09: true if it records the booking.",2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-052,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would three or four one-minute bursts of hard effort a day, built into errands, be easier for me to keep than any planned session?","I plan exercise as sessions. In about 25,000 adults who did no exercise, such daily bursts went with roughly 40% lower mortality. Source: Stamatakis 2022.",try three bursts a day from 5 October,keep planned sessions,news,70,70,86,66,78,explore,Resolved by a later note on the week from 2026-10-05; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-053,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would Semantic Scholar's research feeds, seeded with five étale-cohomology papers, surface a paper I would read by 31 October?","I find papers through my own papers page. Research Feeds recommend new papers from a few you mark. Source: Semantic Scholar.",set up a feed by 9 October,keep searching by hand,news,66,60,84,58,78,explore,"Resolved by a later note: true if I read a paper the feed found.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-054,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Are my own capabilities stronger now than before I ran a fleet of agents?,"A September note asks what should stay stronger once automation is removed. Source: my notes, 26 September.",keep the fleet as it is,name one capability to practise without agents each week,notes,74,62,40,80,86,explore,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note names a capability and judges it; then resolved by that note.,2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-055,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Should a macOS Focus that turns on at 22:00 and hides agent apps do the curfew's work instead of a firstmate hook?","The curfew hook only blocks launches. A scheduled Focus silences apps and notifications on its own. Source: Apple support.",set the Focus tonight,keep the curfew in the hook,news,70,72,86,66,80,explore,"Resolved by a later note on the curfew: true if it records the Focus in use.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-056,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will the first-hand note I endorsed writing tomorrow come before any agent-written note?,"Endorsed tonight at 19%. Source: session 6.",keep the order as planned,write it tonight instead,calibration,66,66,54,72,82,exploit,"Resolved by the first note dated 2026-10-03 or later: true if it is first-hand without #agent-written.",2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-057,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Would working through two solved examples before each beam problem I try teach me more than trying the problems cold?,"When I do work by hand I start with the problem. Studying worked examples beat solving equivalent problems for novices. Source: Sweller 1985.",start the next hand calculation from two worked examples,keep starting cold,news,66,62,82,62,78,explore,Resolved by a later note on a hand calculation; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-058,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Would writing the site's next small interactive page directly in Python with PyScript be quicker for me than JavaScript?,"I write pages in JavaScript. PyScript lets a page run Python from a script tag. Source: PyScript.",write one small page in PyScript by 31 October,keep JavaScript,news,68,62,86,62,80,explore,Resolved by a later note comparing the two; unresolved otherwise.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-059,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Would I be relieved if Calibrator stopped proposing out-of-pattern cards?,"I turned down 24 of session 6's 48 and gave 23% that they beat cards about my plans. Source: session 6.",keep 40 a session,cut them to 20,calibration,74,66,72,92,84,explore,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note says; then resolved by it.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-060,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would the Couch to 5K plan, nine weeks of three guided runs a week in a free app, keep me exercising longer than my own schedule?","I plan exercise myself. Couch to 5K is a free NHS programme for beginners. Source: NHS.",start week one on 5 October,keep my own schedule,news,62,64,82,58,72,explore,"Resolved by a later note: true if week four is done by 2026-11-01.",2026-11-01,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-061,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Should the low threshold of 20 also apply to session 6's answers between 21 and 30 when I act on them?,"From session 7, 20 or less endorses the low action; session 6 was answered under 30. Source: my notes.",treat session 6's 21 to 30 as no endorsement,keep them as weak endorsements,calibration,66,58,58,62,84,exploit,"Resolved by the next reading-rule note: true if it treats them as no endorsement.",2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-062,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would one trip outside with a friend on Sunday 11 October, instead of alone to the new neighbourhood, do more for me?","I endorsed the afternoon alone (90%). Strong social ties raised survival odds by about half across 148 studies. Source: Holt-Lunstad 2010.",invite one friend by 8 October,go alone as planned,news,66,66,76,62,74,explore,Resolved by a note dated by 2026-10-12 on the afternoon.,2026-10-12,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-063,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Should cards that resolve 'by my answer, as a fact' be worded so that I can answer 0 or 100?","Four such cards in session 6 drew 22, 23, 20 and 9, so none resolved. Source: raw.toon.",word them as plain yes-or-no facts,keep them as they are,calibration,70,58,60,58,84,exploit,"Resolved by session 8's cards: true if its fact cards say to answer 0 or 100.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-064,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Would alternating three minutes of fast walking with three slow on the after-lunch walk do more for my fitness than walking at one pace?,"I endorsed a 30-minute walk after lunch. Interval walking raised fitness and lowered blood pressure more than steady walking in a trial. Source: Nemoto 2007.",walk in intervals from 5 October,walk at one pace,news,64,62,84,58,76,explore,Resolved by a later note on October's walks; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-065,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Did I turn down the lecturer card at 4% because a reply might say beamdiag is not useful?,"Session 5 gave 88% that I keep beamdiag from engineers for that reason. Source: my notes.",email one lecturer by 9 October anyway,drop it as decided,calibration,76,70,66,94,82,exploit,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note gives the reason; then resolved by it.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-066,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will I read one landed diff for 20 minutes on Friday 9 October?,"Endorsed tonight (93%). Source: my notes.",make it a standing Friday slot,drop it and say so,notes,64,62,50,74,82,exploit,Resolved by a note dated 2026-10-09 or 2026-10-10 recording the reading.,2026-10-10,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-067,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will the site's own pages take the style guide before any new visualisation lands?,"I gave 99% that they should. Source: my notes.",brief it by 9 October,let the next visualisation go first,project,64,66,46,64,82,exploit,"Resolved by the site on 2026-10-31: true if templates/base.html takes the style guide before a new visualisation lands.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-068,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Is building tools my way into structural engineering partly because hand calculations bore me?,"Candidate effective variable: I learn mathematics by hand and structural engineering by building tools. Source: my notes.",work one textbook beam problem by hand before the next structural tool,keep building tools,synthesis,70,62,40,86,82,exploit,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note gives the reason; then resolved by it.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-069,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Will the hook against writing to Downloads, Desktop and Documents exist by 16 October?","Endorsed tonight (91%). Source: my notes.",leave it to firstmate,brief it myself tomorrow,notes,62,62,50,60,78,exploit,"Resolved by a later note: true if the hook exists by 2026-10-16.",2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-070,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Would spending this month's treat on an experience with a friend rather than a thing lift my mood more?,"My spending is on the fleet. Experiential purchases made people happier than material ones. Source: Van Boven 2003.",book one shared experience by 16 October,skip it,news,62,60,84,60,70,explore,Resolved by a later note on it; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-071,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Is my mind on agents when I am meant to be doing mathematics?,"I endorsed random mind-wandering check-ins for Saturday (95%). Source: session 6.",add 'agents?' to each check-in,keep the check-ins general,calibration,70,58,64,84,80,explore,"Resolved by the check-ins' note: true if most wandering was to agents.",2026-10-04,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-072,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will the savings transfer be set up by 16 October?,"Endorsed tonight (90%); money had been a domain my notes skip. Source: my notes.",keep the date,do it tonight in five minutes,notes,62,66,52,60,72,exploit,Resolved by a note by 2026-10-16 recording it.,2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-073,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Would I answer the since-last cards more honestly if they asked only yes or no?,"I answer 'have I done it' with credences such as 22%. Source: session 6.",make since-last cards plain yes or no,keep the slider wording,calibration,64,54,58,64,82,exploit,"Resolved by session 8: true if its since-last answers are all 0 or 100.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-074,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Would a phone sleep schedule that sets one alarm for all seven days hold the wake-up time better than my own rule?,"I endorsed one wake-up time from 5 October. Phones have a built-in schedule with a wake alarm. Source: Apple support.",set it tonight,rely on my rule,news,62,64,76,58,76,explore,"Resolved by the note on the week from 2026-10-05: true if the wake time held on six of seven days.",2026-10-11,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-075,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Has an endorsed health action of mine happened within the week it was dated?,"My health intentions had been undated; two are now dated from 5 October. Source: my notes.",keep dating them,go back to intentions,notes,64,62,54,76,80,exploit,"Resolved by the note on the week from 2026-10-05: true if it records the mornings done.",2026-10-11,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-076,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Should the Pynite worked example and my site's FEA page use the same model?,"The note suggests it; the pull request is for engineers, the page for my readers. Source: my notes.",build both from one model,keep them separate,synthesis,62,58,64,56,80,explore,"Resolved by a later note: true if both use one model.",2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-077,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will I hold the Hamming list to three problems and say whether I work on any?,"Endorsed tonight (80%), due 9 October. Source: my notes.",keep it to three,let it grow to ten,notes,60,56,54,60,78,exploit,"Resolved by the list's note by 2026-10-09: true if it names three and my work on each.",2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-078,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will the most important problem on my Hamming list be one I am not working on?,"Hamming asked colleagues why they were not on the important problems. Source: my notes.",give it the first October block,keep the blocks for étale cohomology,synthesis,66,64,64,70,80,explore,"Resolved by the list's note: true if the first problem is one I do not work on.",2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-079,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Am I postponing the choice of November's étale computation because committing to one shows how much I do not know?,"The choice moved to an October block; no computation is named yet. Source: my notes, 2 October.",choose it this week,choose it in the October block as planned,notes,66,56,40,62,82,exploit,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note judges it; then resolved by that note.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-080,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will the deploy rule in each brief stop two crewmates deploying at once through October?,"I revised 94 to 14 on making the lock a file. Source: session 6.",keep it in briefs,make the lock a file after all,calibration,64,60,52,64,78,exploit,"Resolved by notes on 2026-10-31: true if no overlapping deploys are recorded.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-081,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Is December's renormalisation-group start best made from Wilson's picture of integrating out scales rather than from beta functions?,"I endorsed starting December from the renormalisation group (92%). Source: my notes.",start from Wilson's picture,start from beta functions,notes,60,52,62,52,72,explore,Resolved by December's first physics note.,2026-12-15,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-082,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Would I finish 120 cards within a day?,"I gave 79% that I would finish 150. Source: session 6.",make session 8 120 cards,keep 100,calibration,60,52,54,52,80,exploit,"Resolved by session 8's export if it has 120 cards: true if all were answered within a day.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-083,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will the paste path stay clean in session 7's export?,"Sessions 5 and 6 came back with no characters to restore. Source: raw.toon.",drop the paste-path test for good,keep it in reserve,calibration,56,48,50,48,74,exploit,"Resolved by session 7's recording: true if no restoration is needed.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-084,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Would one five-minute lightning talk at a Python meetup in Singapore on FEA in the browser bring me one engineer to talk to?,"I turned down crowds; this is one evening. PyData Singapore runs meetups. Source: Meetup.",offer a talk by 31 October,skip it,news,62,58,86,76,70,explore,Resolved by a later note on the talk; unresolved otherwise.,2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-085,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Should fastener-cg's eccentric extension start once the site's pages are restyled, whatever else is waiting?","I gave 12% to starting before 9 October and 3% to Brandt's examples as its test. Source: my notes.",start it right after the restyle,wait for a free crewmate,project,56,58,46,56,76,exploit,"Resolved by the fastener-cg repository: true if work starts within a week of the restyle landing.",2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-086,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Is the next tooling effort for Calibrator better spent on getting me to act than on cards?,"I gave 96% to Calibrator for the next tooling effort. Source: my notes.",point it at acting on endorsed cards,point it at card quality,calibration,62,56,58,62,80,explore,Resolved by a later note on the effort.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-087,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Would I keep a weekly awe walk for four weeks?,"Endorsed tonight (94%), from 5 October. Source: my notes.",keep it to four weeks,make it one walk,notes,54,52,50,52,72,exploit,"Resolved by notes on 2026-11-01: true if four walks are recorded.",2026-11-01,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-088,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will a crewmate remove the private paths the secret scan found by 16 October?,"Endorsed in session 5 at 100%; no note records it done. Source: my notes.",leave it to firstmate,brief it tomorrow,notes,56,56,46,60,74,exploit,Resolved by a note by 2026-10-16 recording the removal.,2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-089,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Would no caffeine after 14:00 change my sleep enough to keep beyond a week?","Endorsed tonight (90%) for the week from 5 October. Source: my notes.",keep it for October,stop after the week,notes,54,52,48,50,72,exploit,Resolved by a later note on the week; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-090,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will the Open questions prune happen by 16 October now that it has moved?,"It moved from 9 to 16 October tonight. Source: my notes.",keep 16 October,drop the prune,notes,52,52,44,56,74,exploit,"Resolved true if a closing note by 2026-10-16 lists each item kept, dated or dropped.",2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-091,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Is Calibrator still the most useful thing I built this month, now that Pynite showed me something new?","I gave 96% tonight. Source: session 6.",keep Calibrator first,give the next effort to the FEA page,calibration,56,52,48,58,78,exploit,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note ranks this month's builds.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-092,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Would I swap the Calibrator post edit for the Pynite pull request in my todos?,"My todos now hold more than eight. Source: my notes.",swap them tonight,keep both,notes,52,54,46,52,74,exploit,"Resolved by a later note on the todo list: true if the swap is recorded.",2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-093,cal-2026-10-02-s7,"Will the October cap of eight new visualisations hold, now that two standalone repositories were split out?","fbd and tampines-food-map got their own repositories on 2 October; ports are exempt. Source: GitHub.",keep the cap,lift it for structural tools,project,50,50,46,52,72,exploit,"Resolved by the catalogue on 2026-10-31: true if no more than eight new visualisations were added from 2026-10-03, ports excepted.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-094,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will my public repositories still number under 70 on 31 October?,"They number 63 tonight. Source: GitHub.",keep the cap as an answer,write it into the brief template,project,48,46,44,50,70,exploit,"Resolved from the GitHub API on 2026-10-31: true if yujieteo has fewer than 70 public repositories.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-095,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Did agent work crowd out the time I meant for the out-of-pattern actions this week?,"Sixteen of them fall due within ten days. Source: session 6.",keep one evening a week free of the fleet,keep evenings open,calibration,58,52,52,70,76,exploit,"Resolved by my answer, as a fact about today.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-096,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Should session 8 again re-ask five cards unchanged?,"Five re-asks moved one card by 20 points this session, against three in session 5. Source: my notes.",keep five re-asks a session,drop re-asks,calibration,50,44,50,48,74,exploit,"Resolved by session 8's cards: true if it re-asks five unchanged.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-097,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will I post the beamdiag question by 9 October now that it is dated?,"I gave 9% that it would be posted while undated. Source: session 6.",keep the date,move it to 16 October,notes,52,52,42,56,74,exploit,Resolved true if a note by 2026-10-09 links the posted question; false otherwise.,2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-098,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Would I rather receive session 8 in the morning than as soon as session 7 is recorded?,"Sessions 6 and 7 both arrived in the evening. Source: raw.toon.",publish session 8 in the morning,publish it as soon as session 7 is recorded,calibration,44,40,46,44,74,exploit,"Resolved by my answer, as a preference.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-099,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will the gym-bag outcome be recorded by 16 October?,"It moved from 9 to 16 October tonight. Source: my notes.",keep 16 October,drop the experiment,notes,46,46,40,50,70,exploit,Resolved true if a note by 2026-10-16 records whether both sessions happened.,2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s7-100,cal-2026-10-02-s7,Will I answer session 7 within a day of its publication?,"Sessions 5 and 6 were each answered within hours. Source: raw.toon.",keep publishing as soon as each is recorded,space sessions by a day,calibration,48,42,40,46,76,exploit,"Resolved by session 7's export: true if exported within a day of publication.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T14:30:00Z"
sources[108]{question_id,source_id,title,url,published_at,retrieved_at}:
  cal-20261002-s7-001,s1,"Answered session cal-2026-10-02-s6 (export of 2 October, recorded in data/calibrator/raw.toon)","https://github.com/yujieteo/calibrator/blob/5ec65cf7b4f8bc47d131fc52a92eff39275008e4/sessions/2026-10-02-s6.toon","2026-10-02T13:45:23Z","2026-10-02T14:20:00Z"
