claims[108]{question_id,source_id,claim}:
  cal-20261002-s7-001,s1,"Session 6 endorsed messaging a friend tonight (95%, s6-026), reconstructing the day tonight (88%, s6-023) and naming the strength days tonight (20%, low action, s6-003)."
  cal-20261002-s7-002,s1,"Pyodide runs CPython in the browser through WebAssembly; micropip installs pure-Python wheels from PyPI, and Pyodide 314.0.7 ships NumPy 2.4.6 and SciPy 1.18.0."
  cal-20261002-s7-002,s2,"PyNiteFEA 3.2.0 is a pure-Python wheel needing NumPy, SciPy, Matplotlib and PrettyTable; in a browser test on 2 October it loaded through Pyodide and solved a 6 m beam (midspan moment 45 kN m = wL^2/8) in 8 seconds."
  cal-20261002-s7-003,s1,"SymPy's Beam class solves reaction loads, shear, bending moment, slope and deflection of beams symbolically, including statically indeterminate ones; it ran in Pyodide on 2 October and returned R1 = 75/2, R2 = 45/2, M1 = -45 for a 6 m propped cantilever under 10 kN/m."
  cal-20261002-s7-004,s1,"Session 6 turned down cold requests to lecturers (4%), a tutor (5%) and Show HN (8%) but endorsed a mentor call (89%) and sending an étale note to a mathematician (83%)."
  cal-20261002-s7-005,s1,"The L-functions and Modular Forms Database is a free online database listing, for each elliptic curve over Q, its local data, Frobenius traces a_p and L-function."
  cal-20261002-s7-006,s1,Session 6 endorsed 19 of its 48 out-of-pattern cards and turned down 24.
  cal-20261002-s7-007,s1,"ccusage reads local usage data from coding-agent CLIs, including Claude Code, and reports daily, weekly, monthly and per-session token use and cost; `npx ccusage@latest` runs it."
  cal-20261002-s7-008,s1,"Session 6 gave 16% to dropping no-mistakes for site code changes (s6-028), against session 5's 85% that Kun Chen's case applies (s5-019)."
  cal-20261002-s7-009,s1,"JupyterLite is a JupyterLab distribution that runs entirely in the browser, built from static files, with Python kernels based on Pyodide."
  cal-20261002-s7-010,s1,"Session 6 endorsed asking one of the people closest to me on 3 October whether I was less present (81%, s6-014)."
  cal-20261002-s7-011,s1,"Datasette Lite runs Datasette entirely in the browser with Pyodide and can load CSV, JSON or SQLite files from a URL for SQL queries."
  cal-20261002-s7-012,s1,"Card s6-020 (100%) showed that a Python FEA library can run on my static site through Pyodide, which I had not known."
  cal-20261002-s7-012,s2,"Of session 6's 48 out-of-pattern cards, 19 drew 80 or more and 24 drew 30 or less."
  cal-20261002-s7-013,s1,The Stacks project is an open-source textbook on algebraic geometry with a chapter on étale cohomology (tag 03N1); each tag page has a comment form.
  cal-20261002-s7-014,s1,Card s6-001 drew 22%; its low action was to hold session 7 until one of session 5's five actions was done.
  cal-20261002-s7-015,s1,"PyR@TE 3 is an open-source Python program that computes the renormalisation-group equations of general gauge theories, gauge couplings up to three loops."
  cal-20261002-s7-016,s1,SymPy's sympy.physics.hep.gamma_matrices module represents Dirac gamma matrices and simplifies their traces and products.
  cal-20261002-s7-017,s1,"Focusmate pairs two people for timed video co-working sessions; a free account gets three sessions a week, reset every Monday."
  cal-20261002-s7-018,s1,"whisper.cpp runs Whisper speech-to-text locally on CPUs, including Apple Silicon, with no network service."
  cal-20261002-s7-019,s1,Card s6-002 drew 23%; its low action was to book the first block for Saturday 3 October.
  cal-20261002-s7-020,s1,"The Brier score decomposes into reliability (calibration), resolution and uncertainty terms."
  cal-20261002-s7-020,s2,The Brier score over all 36 resolved questions is 0.167.
  cal-20261002-s7-021,s1,Pynite's repository has GitHub Discussions open to users.
  cal-20261002-s7-021,s2,"PyNiteFEA 3.2.0 is a pure-Python wheel needing NumPy, SciPy, Matplotlib and PrettyTable; in a browser test on 2 October it loaded through Pyodide and solved a 6 m beam (midspan moment 45 kN m = wL^2/8) in 8 seconds."
  cal-20261002-s7-022,s1,"Session 6 gave 3% that a one-page principles file would replace more than half of a brief's rules (s6-051), against session 5's 82% (s5-028)."
  cal-20261002-s7-023,s1,Reference class forecasting predicts a project's outcome from the actual outcomes of similar past projects rather than from its own plan.
  cal-20261002-s7-023,s2,Session 6 added two dated todos and moved two to 16 October.
  cal-20261002-s7-024,s1,Hypothesis is a property-based testing library for Python that generates test inputs and shrinks failing examples.
  cal-20261002-s7-024,s2,"PyNiteFEA 3.2.0 is a pure-Python wheel needing NumPy, SciPy, Matplotlib and PrettyTable; in a browser test on 2 October it loaded through Pyodide and solved a 6 m beam (midspan moment 45 kN m = wL^2/8) in 8 seconds."
  cal-20261002-s7-025,s1,Deploys run from a local checkout; the playbook names no lock.
  cal-20261002-s7-026,s1,"sectionproperties computes geometric and warping properties of arbitrary cross-sections, including the shear centre, with the finite element method."
  cal-20261002-s7-027,s1,"Three 20-second bouts of vigorous stair climbing, three times a week for six weeks, increased cardiorespiratory fitness in sedentary women."
  cal-20261002-s7-028,s1,Card s6-096 drew 17%; its low action was to pick the squad tonight and stop thinking about it.
  cal-20261002-s7-029,s1,The Lean 4 web editor runs Lean with Mathlib in the browser with no local installation.
  cal-20261002-s7-030,s1,The schedule event runs a GitHub Actions workflow at times set with POSIX cron syntax.
  cal-20261002-s7-030,s2,"The fourth resolution pass, run while recording session 6, resolved two questions."
  cal-20261002-s7-031,s1,A progressive web app can be installed on a device's home screen and run offline with a service worker.
  cal-20261002-s7-032,s1,"Card s6-095, that agent work crowded out time with people this week, drew 85%."
  cal-20261002-s7-033,s1,PR 149 changed the site's maths typesetting to Fira Math through MathJax 4 and merged on 2 October.
  cal-20261002-s7-033,s2,Session 6 endorsed phone screenshots of each restyled page by a crewmate (97%).
  cal-20261002-s7-034,s1,"By 9 October, post the beamdiag hand-calculation question from a crewmate's draft, with the draft by 5 October."
  cal-20261002-s7-035,s1,"handcalcs renders Python calculation code as LaTeX showing symbols, substituted values and results, like a hand calculation."
  cal-20261002-s7-036,s1,The site publishes llms.txt for agents.
  cal-20261002-s7-037,s1,Session 6 gave 89% that a call with someone ten years further along would change my November plans.
  cal-20261002-s7-038,s1,"Others rated observable traits more accurately than the self did, while the self was more accurate on internal traits such as anxiety."
  cal-20261002-s7-039,s1,Screen Time on a Mac reports daily and weekly time spent in each app and website.
  cal-20261002-s7-040,s1,Interleaved (shuffled) practice of mathematics problems produced better test performance a week later than blocked practice.
  cal-20261002-s7-041,s1,The note asks to open the Pynite example pull request by 31 October.
  cal-20261002-s7-042,s1,structuralcodes is an open-source Python library from the fib for structural engineering calculations based on design codes.
  cal-20261002-s7-043,s1,"Session 6 endorsed briefing a crewmate for the token audit on 3 October (84%, s6-022)."
  cal-20261002-s7-044,s1,"The Recurse Center runs 6- or 12-week programming retreats, attendable remotely, with no tuition or fees."
  cal-20261002-s7-045,s1,Agent tooling is taking my mathematics hours this month.
  cal-20261002-s7-046,s1,Items people generated themselves were remembered better than items they only read.
  cal-20261002-s7-047,s1,"Session 6 endorsed twenty minutes of étale reading on each weekday from 5 October (86%, s6-021)."
  cal-20261002-s7-048,s1,giscus embeds comments on static pages and stores them in a repository's GitHub Discussions.
  cal-20261002-s7-049,s1,"Session 6 was imported at 12:48 UTC and exported at 13:45 UTC, 20:48 to 21:45 Singapore time."
  cal-20261002-s7-050,s1,SageMathCell runs Sage code submitted from a web page with no installation.
  cal-20261002-s7-051,s1,Session 6 gave 82% that a monthly meal with one friend does more for my long-term health than the second strength morning.
  cal-20261002-s7-052,s1,"In 25,241 non-exercising adults, about three short bouts a day of vigorous intermittent lifestyle activity were associated with 38 to 40% lower all-cause mortality."
  cal-20261002-s7-053,s1,Research Feeds are an adaptive recommender that learns which papers you care about and recommends new research.
  cal-20261002-s7-054,s1,"Agent tooling should help me become a better human, not merely replace more tasks."
  cal-20261002-s7-055,s1,A Focus on a Mac can turn on by schedule and limit notifications to chosen apps and people.
  cal-20261002-s7-056,s1,Card s6-080 drew 19%; its low action was to write a short first-hand note tomorrow before any agent note.
  cal-20261002-s7-057,s1,Students who studied worked examples learned to solve algebra problems faster and with fewer errors than those who solved equivalent problems.
  cal-20261002-s7-058,s1,PyScript is an open-source platform for writing Python in HTML pages that runs in the browser.
  cal-20261002-s7-059,s1,Card s6-007 drew 23%; 24 of 48 out-of-pattern cards drew 30 or less.
  cal-20261002-s7-060,s1,Couch to 5K is a free NHS app with a nine-week plan of three runs a week for beginners.
  cal-20261002-s7-061,s1,Session 6 is read with 80 and 30; its low endorsements between 21 and 30 are weaker.
  cal-20261002-s7-062,s1,"Across 148 studies, people with stronger social relationships had about 50% greater odds of survival."
  cal-20261002-s7-063,s1,"Cards s6-001 to -003 and -034 resolve by my answer as a fact; they drew 22, 23, 20 and 9 and stay unresolved."
  cal-20261002-s7-064,s1,"In middle-aged and older adults, five months of interval walking (three minutes fast, three slow) raised fitness and lowered blood pressure more than moderate continuous walking."
  cal-20261002-s7-065,s1,"Session 6 turned down emailing three lecturers (4%, s6-006); session 5 gave 88% to keeping beamdiag from engineers in case they say it is not useful (s5-014)."
  cal-20261002-s7-066,s1,"Read one landed diff for 20 minutes each Friday (93%, s6-073)."
  cal-20261002-s7-067,s1,"Restyle the site's own pages next, before any new visualisation (99%, s6-083)."
  cal-20261002-s7-068,s1,I learn structural engineering by building tools.
  cal-20261002-s7-069,s1,"Hook-enforce the rule against writing to Downloads, Desktop and Documents by 16 October (91%, s6-092)."
  cal-20261002-s7-070,s1,People reported that experiential purchases made them happier than material purchases.
  cal-20261002-s7-071,s1,"Card s6-031, setting five random check-ins on Saturday 3 October, drew 95%."
  cal-20261002-s7-072,s1,"By 16 October, set up a monthly savings transfer (90%, s6-069)."
